{"version": 1, "criteria": [{"index": 1, "criterion": "A single retry policy (one package-level classifier plus capped exponential backoff with jitter) is used by both gitcredential.Network and the internal/tracker GitHub REST transport; no other package adds its own retry or backoff loop for GitHub calls, and the duplicated IsNetwork-then-Network wrappers keep calling Network rather than growing their own retries.", "status": "unmet", "evidence": "VALIDATION.md: Independent acceptance review 1: nested fork retry loop"}, {"index": 2, "criterion": "git fetch and ls-remote retry on transient transport failures (connection timed out, could not resolve host, connection reset, remote HTTP 5xx) up to the attempt limit; non-transient failures (authentication, permission, repository not found, rejected or stale --force-with-lease, non-fast-forward) fail on the first attempt with no retry.", "status": "unmet", "evidence": "VALIDATION.md: Focused diagnostic evidence: Git full 5xx classifier"}, {"index": 3, "criterion": "git push retries only when the failure provably happened before the remote received data (DNS or connect phase); interrupted or ambiguous pushes keep today's ErrPublicationUnknown / remote-outcome-unknown result and are never retried, and lease rejections still surface ErrClaimFence with %w wrapping intact.", "status": "met", "evidence": "VALIDATION.md: Independent acceptance review 3; reused developer final-source push/lease/fork/workspace results"}, {"index": 4, "criterion": "GitHub REST GET requests retry on network errors, 502/503/504, and 429 or secondary rate limits (honoring Retry-After within the cap); POST, PATCH, PUT, and DELETE retry only on connect-phase errors where no request was sent.", "status": "met", "evidence": "VALIDATION.md: Independent acceptance review 4; reused developer tracker/shared-policy results"}, {"index": 5, "criterion": "Each retry prints one short line, for example 'GitHub unreachable (connection timed out); retry 2/4 in 8s', through the existing progress.Session.Retry path when a progress session exists and to stderr otherwise; cancelling the context (Ctrl-C) stops the backoff wait immediately.", "status": "met", "evidence": "VALIDATION.md: Independent acceptance review 5; required progress singleton ledger; reused progress race/cancellation results"}, {"index": 6, "criterion": "When retries are exhausted, the error names the operation, the attempts made, and the swarm command to rerun, and all retry output passes through the existing token redaction.", "status": "unmet", "evidence": "VALIDATION.md: Focused diagnostic evidence: REST status exhaustion through go-gh"}, {"index": 7, "criterion": "If checkpoint publication (RecordCheckpoint, RecordPRHead, or the fork checkpoint push) still fails after the developer run, the clean local checkpoint commit and IMPLEMENTATION.md stay in the worktree, the error prints the exact swarm issue reconcile <n> --checkpoint --expected-head <recorded> --candidate-head <local> command, and rerunning swarm issue work <n> on the same claim resumes through that same fenced reconciliation (lease.PrepareCheckpoint / ReconcileCheckpoint) instead of invoking the developer again; a candidate that fails any fence or digest check is preserved and reported, never published or discarded.", "status": "unmet", "evidence": "VALIDATION.md: Independent acceptance review 7; IMPLEMENTATION.md partial recovery handoff"}, {"index": 8, "criterion": "Unit tests using fake git transport, a fake HTTP RoundTripper, and the mock agent cover transient-then-success, exhaustion, non-retryable immediate failure, ambiguous push not retried, lease rejection not retried, cancellation during backoff, Retry-After handling, and a checkpoint-publication failure whose rerun makes zero additional developer invocations; existing adversarial tests pass unchanged.", "status": "unmet", "evidence": "VALIDATION.md: Exhaustive campaign and union proof; three CLI failures; Independent acceptance review 8 missing resume regression"}]}

